atlas interactions

# L5 wiring: each interaction is derived from a real call, include, Makefile or table
# line in the source (see evidence). Class names the strength: invokes (a process is
# started), compiled_or_built_with, names_in_dispatch_table, named_collaborator.

interaction route-arbitrage-invokes-cmd-external-estate
  source route-arbitrage
  destination cmd-external-estate
  relation invokes_binary_by_name
  preserves the destination program's own command line, exit status and output as the only contract the source sees
  drops the destination's stores, in-process state and authority; the source holds only what the child returns
  forbidden_inference the source names the destination's binary or binary-path variable -> every invocation succeeds, or the destination's effect is authorized by the source
  invalidates_on the destination's command line or output format, or the source's lookup of the binary path, changing
  evidence components/BonfyreProject/tools/economic-views.mjs:132 plane = process.env.BONFYRE_EXTERNAL_ESTATE_BINARY || join(repo, "cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/bonfyre-external-e
  binding components/BonfyreProject/tools/economic-views.mjs

